<title>UK: BOE gives money mkt 100 mln stg help at set rates.</title>
<headline>BOE gives money mkt 100 mln stg help at set rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with 100 million stg of assistance at established interest rates to help alleviate a money market shortage forecast at 1.3 billion stg.</p>
<p>The Bank bought bills/FRG totalling 100 million stg for resale on March 12 and 13 at 5-31/32 percent.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.3 BLN    =	    =	    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    100 MLN     =	    =	    =</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG MAR 12/13  100 MLN*    =	    =	    =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
